\cos 5\theta = 16\cos^5 \theta - 20\cos^3 \theta + 5\cos \theta
\] Given that $\cos \theta = \frac{1}{3}$, we can substitute this value into the formula. \[
\cos 5\theta = 16\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^5 - 20\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^3 + 5\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)
\] Simplifying the expression, we get: \[
\cos 5\theta = 16\left(\frac{1}{243}\right) - 20\left(\frac{1}{27}\right) + \frac{5}{3}
\] \[
\cos 5\theta = \frac{16}{243} - \frac{20}{27} + \frac{5}{3}
\] To combine these fractions, we need a common denominator (which is 243): \[
\cos 5\theta = \frac{16}{243} - \frac{180}{243} + \frac{405}{243}
\] Combining the numerators, we get: \[
\cos 5\theta = \frac{16 - 180 + 405}{243} = \frac{241}{243}
\] So, the value of $\cos 5\theta$ is $\frac{241}{243}$. </think> <answer> $\frac{241}{243}$ </answer>

